  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 216 PM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nBeginning Sunday, we transition to more of a zonal upper-level flow \nwith a ridge building west of the Rocky Mountains. High temperatures \nare forecast to remain unseasonably warm for the county warning area \n(CWA) through Tuesday with highs in the 90s to 100s. Sunday is \nforecast to be the hottest day with the entire CWA expected to reach \nabove 100 degrees. A weak cold front moving through Tuesday night \nwill start a cooling trend with high temperatures in the 90s \nWednesday and further dropping in the 80s by Friday.\n\nStarting Sunday evening through at least Friday, there is a \nchance for showers and thunderstorms overnight due to embedded \nshortwave passages. Late Wednesday, we begin to transition to \nmore of a northwest upper-level flow with increased upper-level \nsupport from a jet streak overhead. This will bring chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms overnight Wednesday through the \nremainder of the forecast period. Best chances for showers and \nthunderstorms will be in the late evenings and overnight hours \nWednesday and Thursday with PoPs around 50-70%. Models are \nshowing overall weak instability, but small hail and strong \nwinds are still possible with any storms that form.",
